==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~13.33 seconds<sup>100f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 2~10 seconds<sup>60f~300f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zir Zeal]]s spawn after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zigge]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 20~40 seconds<sup>600f~1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 2~10 seconds<sup>60f~300f</sup>.
*1 [[Zigge]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 2~10 seconds<sup>60f~300f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 90% HP:
**1 [[Kang Roo]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Like with most Zombie stages, getting all of the treasures from the 3 chapters of Empire of Cats before attempting it is highly recommended, as they will make this stage an absolute cakewalk. Any anti-Zombie Gacha Cats you have, such as [[Gardener Cat (Rare Cat)|Gardener Cat]] or [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Wushu Cat]], will also help to make this stage much easier.

If you have none, you can probably just rush the stage with [[Fish Cat (Normal Cat)|Whale Cats]], as actually the threatening Zombies will take a while to spawn, and will burrow under your stack of Whale Cats.

